        "content": "attack - Melee attack an adjacent monster in the given direction. Do NOT call if the target shows `[PET — don't attack]` in ADJAC\ndescend - Descend the down-staircase. You MUST be standing on a '>' tile. Check `=== UNDER PLAYER ===` first — it should say 'stai\nsearch - Search adjacent tiles for hidden passages and traps. Pass `times` to repeat — hidden passages typically need 5-10 search\neat - Eat an edible item from inventory. Pass `item` = substring of the food's description (e.g. 'apple', 'food ration') OR it\nquaff - Quaff (drink) a potion. Pass `item` = substring or letter. If no potion matches, the turn is NOT consumed.\nread - Read a scroll or spellbook. Pass `item` = substring or letter. If no readable matches, the turn is NOT consumed.\npray - Pray to your god (#pray, then 'y' to confirm). Risky if recently used.\nengrave_elbereth - Engrave 'Elbereth' in the dust to scare most monsters. Uses E command.\nkick - Kick (ctrl-D) in a direction. Used to break locks/doors. Pass `direction` (N/NE/.../NW).\nthrow - Throw an item in a direction. Pass `item` (substring/letter) AND `direction`.\npickup - Pick up items on the current tile.\nmove_to - Pathfind to a specific (x, y) tile on the current level. Uses A* over the visible map. The path is precomputed — if a mo\nexplore_and_descend - CLOSED-LOOP mega-skill: automatically explore the ENTIRE current level (revealing rooms/corridors, and SEARCHING dead-en\nadd_note - Write or overwrite a note under a keyed slot. Use this to remember facts that will be useful many turns later: item loca\nrecall - Search your notes for the given query substring. Returns matching (key, text) pairs. Use this when you suspect you've se\npin_objective - Set your current top-level objective. Always rendered into every observation thereafter. Replace as your strategy evolve\nwiki_lookup - Fetch a named NetHack wiki page (e.g. 'cockatrice', 'mine town'). Use when you've identified a specific monster or featu\nwiki_search - Substring-search the NetHack wiki. Returns up to k pages whose title or body contain the query. Use for fuzzy / explorat\n",
        "name": "ipython"
      },
